| info = *Volt expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] to create an electrical energy barrier <u>'''4.25'''</u> meters high and <u>'''6'''</u> meters wide that blocks enemy fire, lasting for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''10 / 15 / 20 / 25''' seconds. Shots fired through the shield made by Volt and his allies gain <u>'''+50%'''</u> {{D|Electricity}} damage and <u>'''+100%'''</u> [[Critical Hit#Critical Damage|critical damage]]. A maximum of <u>'''6'''</u> Electric Shields can be created at a time.
**The [[Critical Hit#Critical Damage|critical damage]] bonus is ''multiplicative'' to all other sources of critical damage, effectively doubling the damage of critical hits.
**The {{D|Electricity}} damage bonus is an ''additive'' bonus that's applied to the weapon's base damage, similar to an elemental mod. For an unmodified weapon that inflicts '''100''' base damage, firing through a shield will increase the total damage to {{Math|100 {{mul}} (1 + 0.5)|bf=y}}. The weapon now inflicts '''100''' base damage and '''50''' {{D|Electricity}} damage.
***Firing through multiple Shields will cause the {{D|Electricity}} damage bonus to stack additively (e.g., firing through '''3''' shields will grant a '''150%''' {{D|Electricity}} damage bonus). The critical damage bonus on the other hand, does '''not''' stack with additional shields.
***The {{D|Electricity}} damage bonus does '''not''' combine with other elemental types to create secondary elements; the weapon will separately proc the elements present on it and {{D|Electricity}} from Electric Shield. {{D|Electricity}} damage bonus from the shield does not increase {{D|Electricity}} status effect damage.
**Casting Electric Shields after reaching the maximum will remove the oldest shield.
*Volt has the ability to pick up one of his Electric Shields through a context action (default {{Keybind|X}}) or by hold-casting the ability. Doing so will cause the shield to decrease in size to <u>'''2.0 m {{mul}} 3.0 m'''</u> and become mobile as a hovering frontal shield that reorients itself to face the player's camera direction, as well as {{D|Ragdoll|Ragdolling}} enemies that come into contact with it. Activating the context action again will place down the shield and revert its size.
**Only '''one''' shield can be equipped at a time.
**Unless forced (e.g., walking into a possessed [[Exolizer]] or into a spear thrown by a [[Kuva Trokarian]]), [[Transference]] will unequip the shield.
**Picking up the shield will prevent Volt from gaining energy from [[Squad Energy Restore]]s, though other sources of energy regeneration over time still work.
*Electric Shield affects things that pass through it differently:
**Melee attacks do <u>not</u> gain bonuses from passing through the shield.
***Projectile based melee attacks such as [[:Category:Warfan|Warfan]] heavy attack projectiles, [[:Category:Gunblade|Gunblade]] shots, {{Weapon|Syam}}'s shockwave, {{Weapon|Tenet Agendus}}'s energy disk, and {{Weapon|Nepheri}}'s fireballs can benefit from Electric Shield's bonuses.
****[[:Category:Glaive|Glaive]] throws do <u>not</u> benefit from Electric Shield.
**AoE attacks require the main projectile to pass through the shield to gain the bonuses; AoE attacks where only the AoE passes through the shield, but not the main projectile, will not gain the bonuses.
**Most Warframe abilities do <u>not</u> gain bonuses from passing through the shield.
***Certain projectile based abilities such as {{A|Fireball}} and {{A|Minelayer|Flechette Orb}} can benefit from Electric Shield's bonuses.
*Prevents self-[[stagger]] from area of effect weapons if the player shoots from behind the shield.

